---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { href, site } from '../config'

const groups = [
  { title: 'Workflow', items: [['install', 'Install & prerequisites'], ['init', 'Initialize a project'], ['config', 'Configure variables & envs'], ['load', 'Load secrets into memory']] },
  { title: 'Operations', items: [['sync', 'Sync & inspect'], ['servers', 'Servers, CI & recovery']] },
]
---
<Base title="Docs" current="Docs" description="Install GitVault v2, initialize a project with gitvault init, configure variables with gitvault config, and inject secrets into RAM with gitvault load.">
  <div class="wrap docs">
    <aside class="side" aria-label="Docs">
      <nav>
        {groups.map((g) => (
          <div class="side-group">
            <h2>{g.title}</h2>
            {g.items.map(([id, t]) => <a href={`#${id}`} data-spy={id}>{t}</a>)}
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="side-group">
          <h2>Reference</h2>
          <a href={href('/security/')}>Security model</a>
          <a href={href('/changelog/')}>Changelog</a>
          <a href={href('/download/')}>Install</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="article">
      <header>
        <span class="eyebrow">Docs · v{site.version}</span>
        <h1 class="t-1">Get started</h1>
        <p class="lead">GitVault v2 is a fast, pure-CLI secrets manager powered exclusively by <code>git</code> and <code>gh</code>. Eliminate <code>.env</code> files in three commands: <code>init</code>, <code>config</code>, and <code>load</code>.</p>
        <details class="mobile-toc">
          <summary>On this page</summary>
          {groups.flatMap((g) => g.items).map(([id, t]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{t}</a>)}
        </details>
      </header>

      <section id="install">
        <h2 class="t-2">Install & prerequisites</h2>
        <p>Both <code>git</code> and the GitHub CLI (<code>gh</code>) must be installed and signed in. GitVault never stores or manages GitHub tokens on its own.</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> gh auth login
<span class="p">$</span> curl -fsSL {site.installScriptUrl} | sh</pre>
        <p>This installs <code>gitvault</code> and its short alias <code>gv</code>. Add the shell wrapper to your profile so <code>gitvault load</code> exports directly into your current terminal session in memory:</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="c"># bash or zsh (~/.bashrc / ~/.zshrc)</span>
eval "$(gitvault shell-init)"

<span class="c"># fish (~/.config/fish/config.fish)</span>
gitvault shell-init fish | source</pre>
      </section>

      <section id="init">
        <h2 class="t-2">Initialize a project (`gitvault init`)</h2>
        <p>Run <code>gitvault init</code> inside any project folder. On your very first run, GitVault uses <code>gh</code> to create a private <code>gitvault-store</code> repository on your GitHub account, asks for a master password, and prints a one-time recovery key.</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> cd ~/projects/shop-api
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault init
<span class="c"># Interactive: pick or create project and default environment</span>

<span class="c"># Or non-interactive with flags:</span>
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault init -p shop-api -e development</pre>
        <p>This creates a minimal, non-secret <code>gitvault.json</code> safe to commit to Git — never a <code>.env</code> file:</p>
        <pre class="code">{'{'}
  "project": "shop-api",
  "environment": "development"
{'}'}</pre>
        <div class="callout"><b>Keep your recovery key safe</b><p>Your recovery key is printed once when the vault store is first created. Save it somewhere safe in case you ever forget your master password.</p></div>
      </section>

      <section id="config">
        <h2 class="t-2">Configure variables & environments (`gitvault config`)</h2>
        <p>Run <code>gitvault config</code> inside your project (or pass <code>-p &lt;project&gt;</code>) for the interactive menu: choose <b>Config variables</b>, select or create an environment, and add, view, delete, copy, or import variables.</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> gitvault config                     <span class="c"># interactive wizard</span>

<span class="c"># Direct CLI shortcuts:</span>
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config set DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/app
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config set API_KEY --value-stdin &lt; key.txt
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config get DATABASE_URL
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config list                <span class="c"># masked by default</span>
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config list --reveal
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config rm API_KEY</pre>
        <p>Already have a <code>.env</code> file? Migrate it into your encrypted vault and remove the plaintext file in one command:</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> gitvault config import .env --delete-source</pre>
        <p>Manage environments directly as well:</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> gitvault config env list
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config env create preview
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config env clone development preview
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault config env delete preview --yes</pre>
      </section>

      <section id="load">
        <h2 class="t-2">Load secrets into memory (`gitvault load`)</h2>
        <p>Secrets are decrypted in RAM and never written to disk as <code>.env</code>. Use <code>gitvault.json</code> automatically, or override with <code>-p</code> and <code>-e</code>:</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="c"># 1. Load into active shell session (with `eval "$(gitvault shell-init)"`):</span>
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault load
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault load -p shop-api -e production
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault unload

<span class="c"># 2. Inject directly into a child process:</span>
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault load -- npm run dev
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault load -p shop-api -e staging -- cargo run

<span class="c"># 3. Export or JSON on stdout for scripts:</span>
<span class="p">$</span> eval "$(gitvault load -p shop-api -e production --export)"
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault load -p shop-api -e production --json</pre>
      </section>

      <section id="sync">
        <h2 class="t-2">Sync & inspect</h2>
        <p><code>init</code> and <code>config</code> commit and push encrypted changes automatically via <code>git</code>. Use <code>sync</code>, <code>projects</code>, and <code>doctor</code> to inspect state or pull changes manually:</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> gitvault sync
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault sync --status
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault projects
<span class="p">$</span> gitvault doctor</pre>
      </section>

      <section id="servers">
        <h2 class="t-2">Servers, CI & recovery</h2>
        <p>In CI or headless servers, authenticate <code>gh</code> (or provide <code>GH_TOKEN</code>) and set <code>GITVAULT_PASSWORD</code> (or pass <code>--password-stdin</code>). Pass <code>--non-interactive</code> so commands never hang waiting for input.</p>
        <pre class="code"><span class="p">$</span> GITVAULT_PASSWORD=… gitvault --non-interactive \
    load -p shop-api -e production -- ./deploy.sh</pre>
        <dl class="options">
          <div><dt>Lock local cache</dt><dd>Run <code>gitvault lock</code> to wipe <code>~/.local/share/gitvault/session.key</code> from disk.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Unlock with recovery key</dt><dd>Run <code>gitvault unlock --recovery-key XXXX-XXXX-…</code> if you forgot your password.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Rotate master password</dt><dd>Run <code>gitvault unlock --change-password</code> to re-wrap the vault key without re-encrypting environments.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <nav class="next" aria-label="Next">
        <a href={href('/security/')}><span>Next</span><b>Security model →</b></a>
        <a href={href('/changelog/')}><span>See also</span><b>Changelog →</b></a>
      </nav>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  const links = new Map([...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-spy]')].map((a) => [a.dataset.spy, a]))
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    for (const e of entries) {
      if (!e.isIntersecting) continue
      links.forEach((a) => a.removeAttribute('aria-current'))
      links.get(e.target.id)?.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true')
    }
  }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -70% 0px' })
  links.forEach((_, id) => { const el = id && document.getElementById(id); if (el) observer.observe(el) })
</script>

<style>
  .docs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 64px; }
  .side nav { position: sticky; top: var(--nav-h); max-height: calc(100vh - var(--nav-h)); overflow-y: auto; padding-block: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px; }
  .side-group { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .side-group h2 { font: 500 0.6875rem/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .side-group a { padding: 6px 12px; margin-left: -12px; border-left: 2px solid transparent; font-size: 0.90625rem; color: var(--ink-2); transition: color 0.15s; }
  .side-group a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .side-group a[aria-current] { color: var(--accent); border-left-color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }

  .article { padding-block: 48px clamp(72px, 10vw, 120px); max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 56px; }
  .article header { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; padding-bottom: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .article section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 24px); }
  .article .t-2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 1.875rem); }
  .article p { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .article .code { font-size: 0.8125rem; }

  .options { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); }
  .options div { padding: 16px 20px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .options div + div { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .options dt { font-weight: 600; }
  .options dd { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .callout { background: var(--warn-bg); border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .callout b { color: var(--warn); }
  .callout p { font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .next { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .next a { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; padding: 20px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); transition: border-color 0.15s; }
  .next a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .next span { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--ink-3); }

  .mobile-toc { display: none; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface); margin-top: 8px; }
  .mobile-toc summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .mobile-toc a { display: block; padding: 8px 16px; color: var(--ink-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .mobile-toc { display: block; }
    .docs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .side { display: none; }
    .options div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .next { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
